    "name_raw": "Patient Strike",
    "definition_type_raw": "Combat",
    "source_book_raw": "Pathfinder Society Primer pg. 8",
    "definition_raw": "Source Pathfinder Society Primer pg. 8\nYour training under the Master of Swords has taught you that a well-timed strike is worth waiting for and that patience will serve you well in the long run.\n\nPrerequisites: Int 13.\n\nBenefit: You can choose to ready an attack as a fullround action instead of a standard action. When you do so, you gain a +2 bonus on your attack roll when your readied action triggers.\n\nNormal: Readying an attack is a standard action and doesn’t grant a bonus on your attack roll.",
